This is the comp at **1 s**, halfway through Title's entrance. "An easing lesson" is still faint because it's partway through its Opacity fade. It's also moving and scaling at the same time.

Right now all three properties change at a **constant speed** from 0.5 s to 1.5 s. That's what linear keyframes do. The text starts moving at full speed at 0.5 s and stops dead at 1.5 s, with no speeding up or slowing down. Position then does the same again from 1.5 s to 3 s. That's why linear motion feels mechanical.

**Easing** makes the motion speed up gently as it leaves a key and slow down as it reaches the next one. That's how real objects move.

**How to do it:**
1. Select Title and press **U** to show its keyframes.
2. Select the keys you want to ease.
3. Choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease**, or press **F9**.
